# OGL 1.0a Architectural Separation

This project uses content licensed under the Open Game License v1.0a. Follow these rules strictly.

## What is Open Game Content (OGC)
Reproduced rules text, mechanics, stat blocks, spells, feats, and other material sourced from SRD documents listed in Section 15 of `/legal`.

## What is Product Identity (PI) — never designate as OGC
- All source code (Ruby, TypeScript, SCSS, etc.)
- AI/engine logic and proprietary game systems
- UI/UX, artwork, branding, layouts
- Original story content, narrative text, adventure premises, NPC descriptions
- Database schemas and API designs

## Separation rules
1. **OGC data belongs in isolated, clearly labelled locations** (e.g. seed files, a dedicated `rules/` data directory, or a separate database table). Never inline OGC rules text into component logic, controllers, or service objects.
2. **Never mix OGC text into proprietary modules.** If a component needs to display OGC content, it should fetch/read it from the isolated data source at runtime.
3. **The `/legal` route and its view are sacred.** Do not gate them behind authentication, do not dynamically alter the OGL text, and do not remove Section 15 entries.
4. **When adding new OGC sources**, always add a corresponding entry to Section 15 in [index.html.erb](mdc:app/views/legal/index.html.erb).
5. **Once content is designated OGC, it is irrevocable.** Be precise and conservative in what you mark as Open Game Content.
